# X-ID data layers

React user/post controls key by numeric X id (`twitterId` / `postId`) when an
X id exists. Handle and npub are display or wire fields, never the entity id.

Unidentified `p:` hops use panel copy *“An external trusted user, X profile not
identified.”* — do not invent a `twitterId`. Id-only users without chrome are
Unknown stubs with a user-initiated `https://x.com/i/user/<twitterId>` link.
Kind 0 name/avatar may appear on those hops with the external disclaimer; never
as mapped-user or operator chrome. Operator chrome is the **current signed-in
X user** (`xIdentities` displayName / handle / iconPath). The header is not a
Nostr switcher; binding completeness uses `xIdentities` plus kind 0.

Translate X id ↔ npub on the backend via `evaluateXIdentityRow` (winning bio /
post / nip39 / 32009). Miss → `undefined`. Pages do not call translation.

Keep `SelectedSubject` and `GRAPH_FOCUS`. Graph clicks keep `OPEN_SIDE_PANEL`.
Normalize mapped `p:` → `user:id` at the backend selection boundary.

Full `XIdentityRecord` / post record for the focused entity;
`XIdentityDisplay` for lists and graph chrome.

Kind `32009` ingest: empty scope or `s=x.com` (`isEligibleXTrustScope`).
Kind `32014` ingest: `s=x.com` required (`isEligibleXRatingScope`). Do not
tighten shared `selectXEligibleTrustEvents`.

Connection UI key is `events.addressKey` (`kind:pubkey:d`), exposed as
`connectionKey`. Do not use `src/graph/trust` `Edge.addressableId`. Do not
edit `src/graph/trust` without explicit permission
(vendored Trust heap; fragile under AI interference).

See [docs/data-layers.md](../../docs/data-layers.md).
